WEBVTT

00:00:03.410 --> 00:00:05.690
An army corps sized group 
of BETA is approaching.

00:00:06.810 --> 00:00:08.350
They're tunneling underground.

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:10.820
The acoustic signatures are increasing.

00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:13.240
We cannot determine their 
numbers or composition.

00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:20.020
No signs of Laser Class BETA.

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:23.440
Repeat, no signs of Laser Class BETA...

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:24.800
What is happening?

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:30.000
<b>BETA Offensive</b>

00:02:04.730 --> 00:02:06.220
We can do this!

00:02:06.220 --> 00:02:07.280
Piece of cake!

00:02:08.770 --> 00:02:10.530
Code 991?

00:02:11.690 --> 00:02:13.890
That close? No way!

00:02:15.680 --> 00:02:17.320
Out of the way!

00:02:19.010 --> 00:02:20.550
There's more of them than an army corps.

00:02:20.550 --> 00:02:21.750
They're advancing towards the base.

00:02:22.110 --> 00:02:23.950
Miss, what do we do?

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:26.460
Bao-Feng 1 to Command Post.

00:02:26.460 --> 00:02:27.500
What's going on?

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:32.290
Command Post! What's happening?

00:02:32.860 --> 00:02:34.550
Lt. Commander Wu, can you hear me?

00:02:34.620 --> 00:02:36.420
What's going on here?

00:02:36.970 --> 00:02:39.540
Was the base wiped out?

00:02:40.020 --> 00:02:41.650
This quickly?

00:02:41.650 --> 00:02:44.510
The only thing that could do 
that would be Heavy Laser Class!

00:02:44.900 --> 00:02:47.020
Bao-Feng 1 to all flights.

00:02:47.020 --> 00:02:48.840
We are leaving the area immediately.

00:02:48.840 --> 00:02:50.430
We will defend the base-

00:02:49.490 --> 00:02:52.680
Base Command to all test flights.

00:02:53.470 --> 00:02:58.590
Base Command is discussing our options 
with UN Dispatch Force Command.

00:02:58.590 --> 00:03:01.470
All test flights are to 
cease their current mission,

00:03:01.470 --> 00:03:03.630
and remain on standby until further note.

00:03:02.020 --> 00:03:03.630
From the Soviets?

00:03:03.630 --> 00:03:05.260
What's going on?

00:03:05.260 --> 00:03:07.600
Zhar Battalion is to continue 
to escort the test flights.

00:03:07.600 --> 00:03:13.180
When all remaining enemies have been 
dispatched, remain on standby in alert status. Over.

00:03:14.130 --> 00:03:16.740
"Discussing"? Do they have time for that?

00:03:16.740 --> 00:03:19.170
What is the Dispatch Force Command doing?

00:03:19.170 --> 00:03:24.190
Miss, does this mean we're taking 
orders from the Soviets for now?

00:03:24.190 --> 00:03:25.430
I think so.

00:03:26.820 --> 00:03:29.440
This is getting pretty weird.

00:03:32.280 --> 00:03:34.730
Jeez, what are we supposed to do?

00:03:34.730 --> 00:03:35.940
Just what you heard.

00:03:36.630 --> 00:03:39.690
Shut up and follow my army's orders.

00:03:39.690 --> 00:03:41.560
Hey, Lieutenant.

00:03:41.940 --> 00:03:44.710
Do you understand the situation here?

00:03:45.240 --> 00:03:47.010
Be quiet, Argos 2.

00:03:47.010 --> 00:03:48.930
You're not the only one who's upset.

00:03:49.380 --> 00:03:50.530
What?

00:03:50.530 --> 00:03:54.710
Yuuya, you say that because 
you don't know anything yet.

00:03:56.150 --> 00:04:00.730
A BETA underground offensive has to be 
dealt with quickly, or it's a real problem.

00:04:04.140 --> 00:04:05.850
Lots of BETA.

00:04:07.270 --> 00:04:07.790
Yes.

00:04:09.920 --> 00:04:12.450
Why can't we go kill them?

00:04:12.940 --> 00:04:13.700
I don't know.

00:04:14.500 --> 00:04:17.200
But we just follow our orders.

00:04:18.290 --> 00:04:20.290
Yeah, you're right.

00:04:21.540 --> 00:04:24.180
The number of vibration 
sources is still increasing.

00:04:24.180 --> 00:04:27.350
These coordinates are within 
range of Laser Class.

00:04:27.870 --> 00:04:30.210
Get our unmanned observer 
drones off the ground!

00:04:30.780 --> 00:04:36.050
The only units we have to defend the base are two 
corps of tanks and one of self-propelled artillery.

00:04:36.050 --> 00:04:39.140
With this few units, we won't 
even be able to slow them down.

00:04:40.340 --> 00:04:43.120
Jeez, how long are they 
going to make us stay here?

00:04:43.560 --> 00:04:46.630
Damn it. Are the guys at the base okay?

00:04:47.050 --> 00:04:48.850
Anyway, you know...

00:04:48.850 --> 00:04:54.120
If we didn't see this coming, that 
means the BETA outsmarted us here.

00:04:54.350 --> 00:04:59.530
That's right. They attack underground 
all the time on the front lines.

00:04:59.950 --> 00:05:02.590
Well, I can see why they'd 
let their guard down.

00:05:02.590 --> 00:05:06.700
Just the fact that there aren't any Laser 
Class here makes life that much easier.

00:05:06.700 --> 00:05:07.550
That's right.

00:05:08.030 --> 00:05:09.720
Shut up.

00:05:10.230 --> 00:05:12.030
I won't let you insult us anymore.

00:05:12.260 --> 00:05:13.500
What's your problem?

00:05:13.500 --> 00:05:17.350
You're the one who keeps badmouthing our ace.

00:05:17.350 --> 00:05:20.130
So you can dish it out but you 
can't take it, is that it?

00:05:20.130 --> 00:05:23.570
That's why you got sneak-attacked 
by the BETA, because you're a wuss.

00:05:23.570 --> 00:05:25.170
Hey, Tarisa.

00:05:25.170 --> 00:05:28.710
There were no moving vibrations 
until right after we launched.

00:05:29.750 --> 00:05:32.800
Or are you saying your own TSFs detected it?

00:05:33.130 --> 00:05:37.170
You're right. The BETA 
move by digging a hole.

00:05:37.170 --> 00:05:39.880
There's no way the sensors 
wouldn't see those vibrations.

00:05:41.270 --> 00:05:44.110
Stop talking down to people when 
you're the ones who screwed up.

00:05:44.630 --> 00:05:46.390
But Lieutenant,

00:05:46.390 --> 00:05:50.900
this is a pretty big screw-up for 
what's supposed to be a veteran force.

00:05:51.480 --> 00:05:54.630
Attacks from underground 
must be common around here.

00:05:54.630 --> 00:05:56.790
This has never happened before!

00:05:57.300 --> 00:05:59.170
In their last big advance a month ago,

00:05:59.170 --> 00:06:00.950
those idiots detected a 
major underground advance

00:06:00.950 --> 00:06:03.610
and didn't stop it until 
they got deep inland...

00:06:04.810 --> 00:06:06.970
An underground advance 
that made it deep inland?

00:06:07.120 --> 00:06:12.180
What? Then you were too lazy to 
close the holes from last time?

00:06:12.180 --> 00:06:14.930
Or left them deliberately?

00:06:16.150 --> 00:06:17.450
Shut up!

00:06:17.450 --> 00:06:20.700
Who would do something like that, 
mocking the souls of the dead?

00:06:22.450 --> 00:06:24.830
Well, sorry. Lieutenant.

00:06:24.830 --> 00:06:27.330
We just forgot ourselves.

00:06:28.190 --> 00:06:33.820
We lost a lot of friends to attacks like 
this when we fought on the front lines.

00:06:36.180 --> 00:06:38.080
Put in the coordinates I give you.

00:06:39.030 --> 00:06:41.070
Unmanned drones are still flying.

00:06:41.420 --> 00:06:44.580
There are no signs of Laser 
Class among the BETA.

00:06:44.850 --> 00:06:48.110
Repeat, there are no signs of 
Laser Class among the BETA.

00:06:48.110 --> 00:06:50.920
The BETA are right on top of us.

00:06:50.920 --> 00:06:52.460
Will the bombers make it in time?

00:06:53.280 --> 00:06:59.480
Heinemann-san, we should withdraw all test 
flights to the retreat point immediately.

00:07:00.040 --> 00:07:01.250
Understood?

00:07:03.790 --> 00:07:06.610
I heard that, Lieutenant. 
And I have no objections.

00:07:07.100 --> 00:07:08.210
Lt. Commander Wu?

00:07:09.750 --> 00:07:13.060
These are the retreat points I've calculated.

00:07:13.060 --> 00:07:14.240
That's fine.

00:07:14.750 --> 00:07:17.060
But given the situation,

00:07:17.060 --> 00:07:20.990
we should have the test flights withdraw 
separately to lower the risk involved.

00:07:22.820 --> 00:07:28.090
The Russian army wishes to ensure the safety 
of the UN test flights as much as possible.

00:07:28.090 --> 00:07:31.250
I suggest sending the Bao-Feng Test Flight 
to point C, and the Argos Test Flight to F.

00:07:31.820 --> 00:07:36.140
We'll have the squads with them now 
escort them to the retreat point.

00:07:36.140 --> 00:07:38.940
If you don't have a problem with 
that, go and give the order.

00:07:42.150 --> 00:07:45.020
Bao-Feng Test Flight is 
to withdraw to point C.

00:07:46.610 --> 00:07:49.760
Tell Argos 1 to withdraw 
to these coordiantes.

00:07:50.260 --> 00:07:55.040
Lt. Sandek, do you not need to tell 
your own flight the withdrawal point?

00:07:55.500 --> 00:07:59.220
My own flight will continue 
to engage BETA group 4

00:07:59.220 --> 00:08:02.180
along with Zhar Battalion 
as part of their exercise.

00:08:02.180 --> 00:08:05.040
In other words, they'll fight to buy us time.

00:08:05.400 --> 00:08:06.580
What?

00:08:06.580 --> 00:08:09.790
Even after they've already 
achieved such a high score?

00:08:13.210 --> 00:08:16.320
Assault Cannons aren't very fun, are they?

00:08:16.320 --> 00:08:17.270
Yes.

00:08:17.710 --> 00:08:19.400
But this is faster.

00:08:19.660 --> 00:08:22.740
I don't intend to tell the Soviet 
Military how to run their plans.

00:08:22.740 --> 00:08:25.640
But what do you mean by buy time?

00:08:25.640 --> 00:08:27.800
There's no sign reinforcements will come.

00:08:28.220 --> 00:08:30.400
We're not waiting for reinforcements.

00:08:30.620 --> 00:08:32.520
We're withdrawing from the base.

00:08:33.190 --> 00:08:35.150
You want us to abandon this base?

00:08:35.560 --> 00:08:36.800
Yes.

00:08:36.800 --> 00:08:39.750
We'll prioritize evacuating 
the UN Dispatch force,

00:08:39.750 --> 00:08:43.400
and send you via air to where 
your test flights are on standby.

00:08:43.910 --> 00:08:47.760
I swear on the motherland's honor that we 
will not let there be a single casualty.

00:08:47.760 --> 00:08:49.090
Please do not worry.

00:08:52.420 --> 00:08:54.430
They're withdrawing that far?

00:08:54.430 --> 00:08:56.780
They're responding surprisingly fast.

00:08:57.390 --> 00:09:00.600
Thankfully, there's no Laser 
Class this time either.

00:09:00.600 --> 00:09:03.290
Which means we should lure them deep inland

00:09:03.290 --> 00:09:05.120
and destroy them with heavy area bombardment,

00:09:05.120 --> 00:09:09.770
and use the TSFs spreading out 
to the rear to destroy them.

00:09:10.560 --> 00:09:11.830
I see.

00:09:11.830 --> 00:09:15.010
Yes. This area does allow 
for a deep formation.

00:09:15.380 --> 00:09:21.310
I do hope you understand that we'll have 
to abandon the test flight's equipment.

00:09:21.310 --> 00:09:22.720
There's no way to carry it.

00:09:23.400 --> 00:09:26.220
At this point we don't have a choice.

00:09:26.220 --> 00:09:28.120
I would like you to reconsider

00:09:28.120 --> 00:09:32.580
in regards to the Imperial Japanese 
prototype we've been loaned.

00:09:32.580 --> 00:09:37.250
I'm sorry, but we don't have any means of 
carrying something that size in this base.

00:09:37.250 --> 00:09:38.970
It's impossible.

00:09:38.970 --> 00:09:43.920
But once we've wiped out the 
enemy you can take it back.

00:09:43.920 --> 00:09:47.230
I see. So this whole thing was their plan?

00:09:48.140 --> 00:09:51.730
Our security forces will escort you.

00:09:52.180 --> 00:09:54.420
Then let's hurry.

00:09:54.420 --> 00:09:56.590
The BETA will be here soon.

00:09:56.590 --> 00:09:59.010
Lt. Dahl, there's no time.

00:09:59.010 --> 00:10:00.080
Give the order.

00:10:00.820 --> 00:10:03.810
All personnel are to withdraw. 
Follow the Soviets' orders.

00:10:03.810 --> 00:10:04.690
Go.

00:10:06.940 --> 00:10:10.510
All XFJ personnel are 
to withdraw immediately.

00:10:11.650 --> 00:10:14.150
Tell the Type 99's mechanics as well.

00:10:15.040 --> 00:10:18.130
Tell them the Imperial Guard 
may abandon it as they see fit.

00:10:18.650 --> 00:10:22.060
Attention XFJ development team.

00:10:22.060 --> 00:10:24.610
All personnel are to withdraw immediately.

00:10:24.610 --> 00:10:26.300
All equipment is to be left here.

00:10:26.300 --> 00:10:28.630
Obey the orders of the 
Soviet Security Personnel.

00:10:29.310 --> 00:10:33.740
Also, the Imperial Guard is to abandon the 
Type 99 Cannon in the manner they see fit.

00:10:33.740 --> 00:10:34.780
Repeat.

00:10:35.320 --> 00:10:36.790
What does that mean?

00:10:43.390 --> 00:10:45.200
We will be escorting you out of the base.

00:10:45.860 --> 00:10:48.450
Please head to Landing Pad 2 immediately.

00:10:50.800 --> 00:10:53.300
Lt. Dahl, come in!

00:10:53.300 --> 00:10:54.200
Lt. Dalh!

00:11:00.920 --> 00:11:02.540
A Code 202 is in effect.

00:11:03.040 --> 00:11:07.190
All personnel are to begin 
evacuation procedure.

00:11:07.190 --> 00:11:10.050
Repeat. A Code 202 is in effect.

00:11:10.050 --> 00:11:11.960
Evacuate?

00:11:11.960 --> 00:11:13.460
We're abandoning the base?

00:11:13.460 --> 00:11:15.080
Hurry, the BETA are almost here!

00:11:16.160 --> 00:11:17.690
Lt. Takamura!

00:11:20.300 --> 00:11:22.280
I'm heading to Hangar 18.

00:11:22.280 --> 00:11:23.670
Are you getting in?

00:11:23.670 --> 00:11:24.490
Wait!

00:11:29.360 --> 00:11:32.340
You saved me, Lieutenant.

00:11:32.340 --> 00:11:34.310
I showed them my ID, I tried everything,

00:11:34.310 --> 00:11:36.870
but they just kept telling 
me to go to Landing Pad 2.

00:11:36.870 --> 00:11:38.520
I didn't know what to do.

00:11:38.520 --> 00:11:40.300
What's happened?

00:11:40.300 --> 00:11:42.520
Have you gotten in touch with the hangar?

00:11:42.520 --> 00:11:43.830
Nope.

00:11:44.380 --> 00:11:47.530
Radio's dead all over the base.

00:11:47.530 --> 00:11:48.790
I thought so.

00:11:48.790 --> 00:11:50.900
I can't get a hold of Command either.

00:11:50.900 --> 00:11:53.330
It's really suspicious, isn't it?

00:11:53.330 --> 00:11:57.370
So I got the hard disk and laptop 
which had the dangerous stuff on it,

00:11:57.370 --> 00:11:59.200
and tried to get to the hangar,

00:11:59.200 --> 00:12:00.600
when the security team caught me.

00:12:01.200 --> 00:12:05.120
Was an evacuation order issued for 
the XFJ project development team?

00:12:05.930 --> 00:12:07.490
Any word from Lt. Dahl?

00:12:07.770 --> 00:12:10.830
The evacuation order came 
once over loudspeaker.

00:12:11.340 --> 00:12:14.890
It was Niram's voice. She 
was saying something odd.

00:12:15.430 --> 00:12:19.890
"The Imperial Guard is to abandon the Type 99 
Cannon in the manner they see fit," or something.

00:12:20.250 --> 00:12:21.050
What?

00:12:21.530 --> 00:12:23.230
Strange, huh?

00:12:23.230 --> 00:12:25.910
The Type 99's under Imperial 
Army jurisdiction.

00:12:25.910 --> 00:12:29.360
Ibrahim wouldn't make that mistake.

00:12:29.610 --> 00:12:30.690
That's right.

00:12:31.710 --> 00:12:34.540
Lt. Dahl was trying to tell 
me that something's up;

00:12:34.540 --> 00:12:38.440
that the Soviets are after the Type 99.

00:12:38.440 --> 00:12:40.870
They're going to take it for themselves?

00:12:41.320 --> 00:12:44.700
That explains why they were so obsessed 
with getting Ensign Bridges out there.

00:12:45.050 --> 00:12:46.150
I see.

00:12:46.150 --> 00:12:50.790
If the 94 Second was still here 
it could take the Type 99 with it.

00:12:50.790 --> 00:12:51.530
Probably, yes.

00:12:52.210 --> 00:12:56.110
That means things for him and 
the others at the command post

00:12:56.110 --> 00:12:59.810
were bad enough that he had to use a code.

00:13:00.260 --> 00:13:01.550
Don't worry.

00:13:01.550 --> 00:13:06.650
If they thought they could take it by force 
they wouldn't go through all this trouble.

00:13:06.650 --> 00:13:09.190
They don't want to make 
enemies out of the UN.

00:13:09.940 --> 00:13:14.160
There were a lot of things that seemed 
strange about this whole mission.

00:13:14.160 --> 00:13:17.450
Both you and Lt. Dahl thought something 
was up from the start, didn't you?

00:13:17.840 --> 00:13:19.040
Yes.

00:13:19.040 --> 00:13:21.620
But to make all this happen...

00:13:22.250 --> 00:13:25.200
No, is that possible?

00:13:25.200 --> 00:13:26.540
What?

00:13:27.000 --> 00:13:28.940
No, it's nothing.

00:13:30.790 --> 00:13:34.940
Sergeant Lowell, take care of 
the classified data for me.

00:13:34.940 --> 00:13:37.920
I'll finish it quick and meet up with you.

00:13:37.920 --> 00:13:38.820
No.

00:13:39.370 --> 00:13:42.150
As soon as you're done with the 
data head to Landing Pad 2.

00:13:42.150 --> 00:13:43.020
But...

00:13:43.430 --> 00:13:47.280
The only thing we can do at this 
point is blow up the Type 99.

00:13:48.530 --> 00:13:50.560
Then the more people you have the better.

00:13:51.000 --> 00:13:55.380
And it's unreasonable for the project lead 
to do something so dangerous herself.

00:13:55.720 --> 00:13:58.340
I'm the only one who knows 
the self-destruct code.

00:13:58.340 --> 00:14:00.420
Then tell it to me.

00:14:02.910 --> 00:14:05.800
I'll admit you're right 
that it's unreasonable.

00:14:05.800 --> 00:14:09.060
But the Japanese don't act on reason alone.

00:14:09.650 --> 00:14:11.190
Yeah, that's right.

00:14:11.190 --> 00:14:14.260
The Japanese are well... I 
don't know how to put it.

00:14:15.220 --> 00:14:18.000
Yuuya was just like that.

00:14:20.890 --> 00:14:21.970
Lieutenant?

00:14:22.430 --> 00:14:26.990
As long as we have you, 
that data, and Bridges,

00:14:26.990 --> 00:14:29.060
we can make the XFJ project a success.

00:14:29.300 --> 00:14:30.040
Wait!

00:14:32.380 --> 00:14:35.310
Don't get any weird ideas, Princess Yui.

00:14:37.520 --> 00:14:40.080
More vibration sources.

00:14:40.080 --> 00:14:42.620
The base has issued a Code 202.

00:14:43.140 --> 00:14:44.780
It's begun?

00:14:45.100 --> 00:14:48.540
What about our back-up plan 
for the worst-case scenario?

00:14:48.740 --> 00:14:52.890
Yes sir. All bombers are on 
standby and ready to launch.

00:14:52.890 --> 00:14:55.930
They can be in the air within five 
minutes of being given the order.

00:14:56.430 --> 00:14:58.740
So the die has been cast...

00:14:59.550 --> 00:15:03.690
Show us you can do it, Comrade Sandek.

00:15:04.640 --> 00:15:07.210
For your own sake.

00:15:11.800 --> 00:15:13.330
There's just too many of them!

00:15:13.330 --> 00:15:15.130
We won't be able to last much longer!

00:15:15.410 --> 00:15:18.650
At least last until the UN forces get out!

00:15:21.550 --> 00:15:23.000
Wait! Wait, please!

00:15:23.000 --> 00:15:23.990
Get on the next one!

00:15:28.070 --> 00:15:30.140
Please hurry, Lt. Dahl.

00:15:30.730 --> 00:15:33.660
You needn't worry about Lt. Takamura.

00:15:36.560 --> 00:15:38.460
A Code 202 is in effect.

00:15:38.460 --> 00:15:42.250
All personnel are to begin 
evacuation procedure.

00:15:42.400 --> 00:15:44.670
Repeat. A Code 202 is in effect.

00:15:42.830 --> 00:15:44.160
Lt. Takamura, yes?

00:15:44.670 --> 00:15:49.620
I am Sergeant Orloff. I have been ordered 
to help evacuate the XFJ personnel.

00:15:50.090 --> 00:15:52.660
Everyone has already safely evacuated.

00:15:53.100 --> 00:15:55.030
I thank you for your swift response.

00:15:55.620 --> 00:15:57.690
Please withdraw as well.

00:15:57.690 --> 00:16:01.010
No. Securing your safety is 
part of our mission as well.

00:16:01.470 --> 00:16:02.750
I see.

00:16:02.750 --> 00:16:04.550
Let's go then. It's this way.

00:16:05.120 --> 00:16:08.630
Just like you, I have a mission of my own.

00:16:08.630 --> 00:16:11.070
I cannot leave without completing it.

00:16:11.070 --> 00:16:12.170
It won't take long.

00:16:12.170 --> 00:16:13.290
Don't get in my way.

00:16:19.700 --> 00:16:21.950
So their radios work, huh?

00:16:26.520 --> 00:16:27.400
An error?

00:16:27.400 --> 00:16:28.060
No way.

00:16:28.680 --> 00:16:29.820
Lieutenant!

00:16:29.820 --> 00:16:31.120
The Soviets, huh?

00:16:31.890 --> 00:16:34.090
The BETA are within 6 klicks of us.

00:16:34.090 --> 00:16:35.500
Please hurry.

00:16:35.500 --> 00:16:36.790
That's the last helicopter.

00:16:37.260 --> 00:16:43.300
Sergeant, I've activated the cannon's 
self-destruct mechanism to maintain our secrets.

00:16:44.320 --> 00:16:47.280
It will probably wipe everything 
out in a 2km radius.

00:16:47.280 --> 00:16:48.860
But we can take the BETA with us.

00:16:48.860 --> 00:16:50.270
A 2km radius?

00:16:50.270 --> 00:16:51.200
That large?

00:16:51.200 --> 00:16:54.570
Run! If we don't get away 
the shock wave will get us.

00:16:54.570 --> 00:16:55.890
Follow her!

00:16:55.890 --> 00:16:58.830
Sergeant! Order the helicopter 
to take off as fast as you can.

00:16:59.930 --> 00:17:03.270
Hurry! We'll be caught in the blast! Get on!

00:17:04.690 --> 00:17:05.330
Take off!

00:17:07.880 --> 00:17:08.450
Lieutenant?

00:17:09.330 --> 00:17:10.870
I forgot something.

00:17:19.540 --> 00:17:20.670
Who are you?

00:17:20.670 --> 00:17:23.180
Corporal Yamamoto. I work on the Type 99.

00:17:23.710 --> 00:17:26.700
I was doing maintenance work so they 
didn't see me. I've been hiding.

00:17:27.120 --> 00:17:30.790
I see. Unfortunately it's 
too late to evacuate.

00:17:30.790 --> 00:17:32.140
Prepare yourself.

00:17:32.140 --> 00:17:36.680
Yes. I was planning on staying 
behind to destroy this.

00:17:37.860 --> 00:17:39.130
I'm sorry.

00:17:39.130 --> 00:17:41.410
I was the only one who needed to stay.

00:17:41.410 --> 00:17:43.070
Not at all!

00:17:43.070 --> 00:17:44.320
More importantly, Lieutenant,

00:17:44.320 --> 00:17:46.970
the Soviets have done something 
to the self-destruct mechanism.

00:17:47.350 --> 00:17:51.120
We need the maker's master code 
to recover from that error.

00:17:51.120 --> 00:17:52.960
We can't make it self-destruct like this.

00:17:53.370 --> 00:17:57.690
But we must destroy it ourselves.

00:17:57.690 --> 00:18:00.950
We need to think of some 
way to get out of this.

00:18:02.010 --> 00:18:05.490
Just to confirm, this order is not the 
result of confusion in the chain of command?

00:18:05.770 --> 00:18:06.830
Yes.

00:18:06.830 --> 00:18:12.070
The Zhar Battalion's new orders are to 
deploy 5000 meters forward from the supply base.

00:18:12.310 --> 00:18:14.670
You're sure about that order, right?

00:18:15.120 --> 00:18:19.140
I'm not dying to defend an abandoned 
base because somebody screwed up.

00:18:20.380 --> 00:18:21.870
Commander Latrova,

00:18:21.870 --> 00:18:25.790
I am Commander Rogofsky of the 
Central Strategic Research Corps.

00:18:26.600 --> 00:18:30.510
The order you've been given is the correct 
one, and has been approved by central command.

00:18:30.510 --> 00:18:32.780
Execute it immediately.

00:18:33.110 --> 00:18:34.940
I apologize.

00:18:34.940 --> 00:18:36.800
We just finished babysitting our guests

00:18:36.800 --> 00:18:40.210
and suddenly we were ordered out 
here in the middle of nowhere.

00:18:40.210 --> 00:18:42.570
I thought there might have been some mistake.

00:18:42.940 --> 00:18:46.310
Those coordinates are where the second 
wave of BETA are expected to appear.

00:18:46.690 --> 00:18:52.670
We sent you there because you performed so 
splendidly in the underground attack last month.

00:18:53.670 --> 00:18:56.070
Last time, huh?

00:18:56.670 --> 00:18:59.410
It seems you didn't learn 
a thing from that, though.

00:19:00.220 --> 00:19:01.810
What do you mean?

00:19:02.080 --> 00:19:04.920
The BETA appeared at almost exactly 
the same point as last time.

00:19:05.650 --> 00:19:07.960
We took so much damage last time,

00:19:07.960 --> 00:19:11.190
why did we leave the holes they 
made instead of sealing them?

00:19:11.190 --> 00:19:14.900
Ask your own commander, not me.

00:19:15.460 --> 00:19:19.920
Any further delay and I'll have to tell 
the party you were disobeying orders...

00:19:21.760 --> 00:19:24.180
Zhar 1 to all units. Begin moving.

00:19:24.870 --> 00:19:27.000
We're going to protect your nest.

00:19:27.000 --> 00:19:27.670
Roger.

00:19:28.120 --> 00:19:29.960
Zhar 2, you heard that right?

00:19:29.960 --> 00:19:32.260
We'll meet up with the escort 
flights at the rendezvous point.

00:19:32.260 --> 00:19:33.270
Hurry.

00:19:33.270 --> 00:19:34.430
Zhar 2, roger!

00:19:34.900 --> 00:19:36.990
Listen. Stay put.

00:19:36.990 --> 00:19:37.940
This is an order.

00:19:42.410 --> 00:19:47.380
We sure were lucky that the Zhar Battalion's 
second in command was our escort.

00:19:47.380 --> 00:19:50.320
When she gets pissed off she doesn't 
pay attention like she should.

00:19:50.630 --> 00:19:52.980
That got us the information 
we wanted, though.

00:19:52.980 --> 00:19:57.500
Hey, is this really the time for playing spy?

00:19:57.500 --> 00:20:01.580
I took a little peek at her 
TSF's log via the data link.

00:20:01.580 --> 00:20:07.630
The major BETA landing Lt. Commander Ivanov 
accidentally told us about matches the records.

00:20:08.900 --> 00:20:12.970
Looks like that's when the 
Mobile Infantry took a big hit.

00:20:14.260 --> 00:20:17.220
That's really important, but they didn't 
mention it during the briefing at all.

00:20:17.840 --> 00:20:20.830
Somebody in the Soviet Military 
was hiding it from us.

00:20:20.830 --> 00:20:25.350
Probably to keep us from realizing 
that they set this whole situation up.

00:20:26.420 --> 00:20:30.240
They deliberately invited the BETA 
into a critical frontline base?

00:20:30.550 --> 00:20:34.990
They probably didn't seal 
the holes on purpose.

00:20:34.990 --> 00:20:38.610
That's why the BETA were able to follow 
the same path they did a month ago.

00:20:38.900 --> 00:20:40.360
I see.

00:20:40.360 --> 00:20:43.990
That's why we couldn't detect them digging.

00:20:43.990 --> 00:20:46.010
But why? It doesn't make any sense.

00:20:46.300 --> 00:20:47.830
I don't know.

00:20:47.830 --> 00:20:54.050
But it's true that Lt. Dahl and Lt. Takamura 
were suspicious of this whole mission.

00:20:56.250 --> 00:20:57.990
Two heavy transport helicopters.

00:20:57.990 --> 00:20:59.430
They're part of the base's forces.

00:20:59.880 --> 00:21:02.310
Can you hear me, Argos 1?

00:21:02.520 --> 00:21:03.640
Vincent?

00:21:03.640 --> 00:21:04.850
That's you, isn't it Vincent?

00:21:04.850 --> 00:21:07.580
This is Argos 1. Did you 
evacuate by helicopter?

00:21:07.580 --> 00:21:10.070
Yuuya! Damn, I finally made it through!

00:21:10.560 --> 00:21:11.690
Are you okay?

00:21:11.690 --> 00:21:14.090
Where are the others? Are they with you?

00:21:14.090 --> 00:21:18.220
The mechanics and staff, along with the 
Imperial Army personnel are with me.

00:21:18.220 --> 00:21:21.960
Ibrahim and the other higher-ups are 
heading to another withdrawal point.

00:21:22.250 --> 00:21:23.880
Glad to hear it!

00:21:24.200 --> 00:21:25.530
Listen to me!

00:21:25.530 --> 00:21:27.130
We've got a problem!

00:21:27.410 --> 00:21:29.980
Lt. Takamura is still at the base!

00:21:29.980 --> 00:21:31.020
What?

00:21:31.020 --> 00:21:33.180
She was trying to destroy 
the Type 99 Cannon...

00:21:34.140 --> 00:21:37.000
Vincent! Hey, Vincent!

00:21:40.800 --> 00:21:43.180
Lieutenant, this is the last round.

00:21:43.970 --> 00:21:44.900
It's no good.

00:21:44.900 --> 00:21:47.650
The core parts are too solid and 
have too high a melting point.

00:21:48.210 --> 00:21:53.950
Simultaneously detonating the bullets with jet 
fuel won't be enough to destroy the core modules.

00:21:54.310 --> 00:21:59.330
Corporal, can we at least get the 
covers off the parts that are classified?

00:21:59.330 --> 00:22:01.970
I specialize in the electronics.

00:22:01.970 --> 00:22:04.100
I couldn't do it with the time we have left.

00:22:04.810 --> 00:22:05.820
Alright.

00:22:05.820 --> 00:22:07.590
Continue getting ready to blow it up.

00:22:07.590 --> 00:22:08.750
I'm sorry.

00:22:09.600 --> 00:22:10.970
What do I do?

00:22:10.970 --> 00:22:12.240
What can I do?

00:22:13.530 --> 00:22:17.000
He never gave up no matter 
how hard things got.

00:22:18.680 --> 00:22:21.260
Yuuya Bridges...

00:22:23.830 --> 00:22:27.170
Why am I thinking about 
him at a time like this?

00:24:07.380 --> 00:24:10.250
Weren't you going to make 
the XFJ project a success?

00:24:10.860 --> 00:24:13.150
I don't know what you're 
sacrificing yourself for,

00:24:13.150 --> 00:24:17.170
but I don't want you just leaving me!

00:24:17.140 --> 00:24:24.390
<b>The End of a Deadly Battle</b>

00:24:19.510 --> 00:24:21.730
Next time on Total Eclipse:

00:24:22.230 --> 00:24:23.970
The end of a deadly battle
